WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.057
A strong controller mixes deterministic rules with model-assisted judgment.

00:00:05.057 --> 00:00:14.392
Use normal code for order I D extraction, permissions, date comparisons, known categories, and exact thresholds.

00:00:14.392 --> 00:00:21.592
Use model judgment for ambiguous intent, semantic classification, evidence interpretation,

00:00:21.592 --> 00:00:24.042
or flexible language transformation.

00:00:24.613 --> 00:00:26.614
Here is a simple example.

00:00:26.614 --> 00:00:33.084
A regular expression extracts order number one zero four two from the user's text.

00:00:33.084 --> 00:00:40.749
Then a semantic classifier decides whether the user wants return eligibility, refund status,

00:00:40.749 --> 00:00:43.784
or a general policy explanation.

00:00:43.784 --> 00:00:46.414
The first task is exact.

00:00:46.414 --> 00:00:48.819
The second task involves meaning.

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:55.882
This hybrid approach gives the model work it is good at while keeping hard constraints in software.

00:00:55.882 --> 00:00:59.340
It also reduces unnecessary model calls.
